{"skill":{"slug":"eastmoney-fin-search","displayName":"eastmoney skills"},"version":{"version":"1.0.5","createdAt":1773818355791,"changelog":"- Skill name changed from \"mx_search\" to \"eastmoney_fin_search\"\n- Added `required_env_vars` and `credentials` sections to the skill manifest for clearer API key requirements\n- Updated description and metadata formatting at the top for better structure and clarity\n- No code or functionality changes detected","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"mx_search.py","size":6812,"sha256":"f151de6020ee4757e5ade67cf1db55d6ba86c14ada3cf76a786c1148af4a8c92","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3138,"sha256":"9ba3c72be35efcfdd7fab58ad0f943e30489b32d229936048946b1b2e7bc816b","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2044,"sha256":"26091d92113cd83a27427a97c9f294d348248d9e13723b72eb3471abf40e3b55","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789171516961,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"80e39778633010e2fa3cf6688340e5b25b5076bc48e6f6b578239b4eea1c64e8","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/80e39778633010e2fa3cf6688340e5b25b5076bc48e6f6b578239b4eea1c64e8","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780085977546},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":44,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":6,"checkedAt":1789171516961},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill coherently provides disclosed financial news search using an API key, with expected network calls and local result files, but users should avoid sensitive queries and untrusted output folders.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Reading one named environment variable and sending the query to the documented HTTPS API is proportionate for this search integration, but financial queries may reveal sensitive interests or research intent.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No installer, dependency installation, tool wrapping, or automatic startup behavior was found; the package contains a markdown skill file and a Python helper script.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill clearly discloses MX_APIKEY, the external API domain, and output files, but it does not include fine-grained runtime permission metadata limiting egress or file writes.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The script automatically saves extracted text and raw JSON results to a disclosed default output directory or a user-supplied directory; this is expected but creates retention and file-handling considerations.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is financial information search, and the artifact implements that by sending the user query to the documented Eastmoney endpoint and formatting the returned financial news, reports, and announcements.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending financial search queries to the documented Eastmoney API using MX_APIKEY. Avoid putting confidential client data or proprietary trading intent in queries, store outputs in a private trusted directory, and do not run it with elevated privileges or shared writable output paths.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The scanner's least-privilege concern is valid as a hardening note, but the artifact discloses the credential, endpoint, and output behavior and does not show hidden or unrelated authority.\n[E1] expected: Sending the user query to mkapi2.dfcfs.com is the core search function and is disclosed in SKILL.md; users should still treat query text as data shared with an external provider.\n[SQP-2] expected: Local saving of text and raw JSON is implemented and disclosed in the configuration section; it is a privacy/retention note rather than hidden persistence.\n[SDI-2] expected: The environment API key is declared in SKILL.md front matter and configuration, so the artifact does not support the claim that credential handling is undisclosed.\n[SDI-1] expected: Persisting search results is broader than pure retrieval but is explicitly documented with filenames and the default output directory.\n[T09] unexpected: The predictable output filenames and normal write mode create a symlink-overwrite risk if a user chooses an output directory writable by an attacker; this is a real implementation hardening issue but does not indicate malicious intent.\n[T09] unexpected: API-provided text is printed without terminal control-sequence sanitization, which could allow misleading terminal output if upstream content is hostile; this is a display-safety issue rather than evidence of deception by the skill.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789171516961}}}}}